WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:05.840
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, since comic
con was last weekend and Korra just went digital

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:09.080
I’m going to be combining my episode 8 and
9 reviews in this video.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.380
I’ll also explain a little more what is
happening with the show.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:11.380
A lot of you are still asking a lot of questions
about what the deal is.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:14.040
But don’t worry, it’s not bad, nothing
bad is happening.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.349
Also I have a bunch of stuff to giveaway.

00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:19.310
So I’ll announce which people won at the
end of this video.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:23.170
In case you’re just finding me for the first
time.

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:24.850
I do Korra videos every week.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:28.580
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:36.739
I want to focus mostly on episode 9 but real
quick some things worth mentioning about episode

00:00:36.739 --> 00:00:37.960
8.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:39.949
Best fight scene all season.

00:00:39.949 --> 00:00:41.760
Team Zaheer versus Team Korra.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:45.239
I feel like the Red Lotus people are so well
trained, Korra is going to keep getting her

00:00:45.239 --> 00:00:47.519
ass handed to her in combat.

00:00:47.519 --> 00:00:50.129
It’s like fighting a bunch of Unalaq’s
at once.

00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:53.260
Meaning Korra will have to find a non-combat
solution to defeat Zaheer.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.179
It’s not going to end in a bending match.

00:00:55.179 --> 00:00:56.179
Fire Ferrets style.

00:00:56.179 --> 00:01:00.710
But I do think that the metal bending foozball
game will come back in an interesting way.

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:02.339
Or at least I hope it does.

00:01:02.339 --> 00:01:05.940
Just imagine Bolin bouncing metal discs all
over a bunch of bad guys or Dai Lee Agents.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:09.170
I still think he’ll learn to metal bend
at some point this season.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:11.130
Even though Aiwe turned out to be the obvious
traitor.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:12.570
I still feel like Souyin is involved somehow.

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:14.480
Like she’s part of the Red Lotus.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:16.290
Technically they’re not an evil organization.

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:21.049
But she is way to sanguine about Korra’s
safety, especially letting her go so quickly.

00:01:21.049 --> 00:01:23.850
And that person in her circus photo from when
she was younger.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.700
Looks like Zaheer wearing clown makeup.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:30.380
She also talked about hating the idea of the
Earth Kingdom still having a queen.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:34.020
So even if she’s not a full on Red Lotus
member, she’s probably a collaborator.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.350
Which is just as bad.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:39.680
As for Varrick, I feel like his magnetic technology
will come in handy in an unexpected way.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.869
Like he’ll help Team Korra take down the
metal benders if it turns out Souyin really

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:44.679
is working with the Red Lotus.

00:01:44.679 --> 00:01:47.920
Aside from that his Airbender finding device
feels like a dead end.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.619
The only way I see it being important is in
Korra using it to find an airbender in a giant

00:01:52.619 --> 00:01:53.619
group of people.

00:01:53.619 --> 00:01:56.700
Like find a hidden airbender who’s trying
to evade them.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:57.700
Like Zaheer.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:00.840
I didn’t like the pacing of the episode
quite as much as some of the others so I gave

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:05.780
it a B. Overall the animation overall was
amazing, but the animation during the fight

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:06.840
scenes was brilliant.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:09.369
Studio Mir has done an amazing job this season.

00:02:09.369 --> 00:02:12.480
So every time I want to give Mike, Bryan and
the cast a high five.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.770
I have to remember to give Studio Mir a high
five.

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:16.770
Moving on to Episode 9.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:18.341
I’ll do this a little bit more like my traditional
reviews with top 5 moments just because I

00:02:18.341 --> 00:02:19.959
feel like we got so much more of the plot
explained to us.

00:02:19.959 --> 00:02:21.959
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
it yet.

00:02:21.959 --> 00:02:26.950
I’ll explain where and how to watch episodes
at the end of the review.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:28.350
Starting with top 5 moments.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:29.569
Here we go.

00:02:29.569 --> 00:02:32.150
Number 5 - Bolin’s Fandom

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:35.510
I feel like you could single out several Bolin
moments, but they’re all about him being

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:36.840
a mover star.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.390
You can tell he really misses it.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:43.800
Once Book 4 is over and they settle down and
hopefully start families of their own, I’d

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:48.590
like to see Bolin start his own Mover studio.

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:52.420
His superfans were by far the funniest moment
in the episode and while Mike and Bryan and

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:54.260
the writers were responsible for the dialogue.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:57.739
I wonder if they’re poking fun at their
fans or at Janet Varney’s fans.

00:02:57.739 --> 00:03:00.299
They’re not mean or anything, it’s all
just meant to be silly.

00:03:00.299 --> 00:03:03.099
But I’ve met people like that.

00:03:03.099 --> 00:03:05.750
The thing that made it even funnier was that
they animated them as these hulking muscular

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:06.750
people.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:10.439
Like street thugs who turned out to be harmless
superfans.

00:03:10.439 --> 00:03:13.200
Maybe that’s the way Mike and Bryan see
the Korra fandom.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:16.909
Really intense looking, but secretly harmless.

00:03:16.909 --> 00:03:21.920
You can let me know if you agree with that
but if any of you go to New York Comic Con

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:27.640
and you get a chance to take a picture with
Janet Varney or PJ Byrne please try to get

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:34.950
them to re-enact that scene.

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:38.540
It would be like the most perfect animated
gif of the real life Korra actors ever.

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:43.700
Going back to familiar territory now, Number
4 - The Desert Oasis Animation

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:46.760
This isn’t really a moment specifically,
it’s just the animation during all the desert

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:47.760
oasis scenes.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.930
When you see Mako and Bolin entering, Korra
on the hill looking down.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:53.330
It’s so beautiful the way they did it.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:04:00.150
I know a lot of you guys who subscribed to
me back when I was doing Book 2 videos really

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:02.620
didn’t like the animation at the time.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:07.510
Supposedly the only reason Studio Mir didn’t
animate all of Book 2 was just schedule conflicts

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:08.760
and manpower.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:12.400
During the comic con panel Bryan Konietzko
even said that Studio Mir had to call in some

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:14.409
help to animate book 4 stuff.

00:04:14.409 --> 00:04:15.780
They’re in the middle of that right now.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:18.549
It takes an army of people to do animation.

00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:20.130
Just as a point of comparison.

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:22.160
When they were making the simpsons movie at
fox a couple years ago.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:28.910
Matt Groening said that the Simpsons people
between the tv show and the movie, hired every

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:33.610
single animator in hollywood that wasn’t
already working for another animated show.

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:35.850
That’s a shitload of people.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:39.990
but now let’s start peeling open the Red
Lotus, Number 3 - Korra and Zaheer meet in

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:41.220
the spirit realm

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:46.259
Zaheer is skyping with the other Red Lotus
members in the spirit realm.

00:04:46.259 --> 00:04:47.635
I feel like the Red Lotus has probably been
using that as a global communication device

00:04:47.635 --> 00:04:48.730
for their entire existence.

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:53.330
I also liked how Zaheer stalled Korra by luring
her into a long explainer speech about who

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:54.330
they were.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:57.550
He didn’t really explain his plan but I’m
going to separate a few bits from the spirit

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:59.850
realm scenes.

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:01.840
As for Aiwe, don’t feel too bad for him.

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:04.720
Remember that Zhao is also stuck in the fog
of lost souls.

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:07.130
They can always meetup and talk about how
much they hate the Avatar.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:08.729
Maybe play some spirit realm pai sho.

00:05:08.729 --> 00:05:11.320
If Iroh can have tea parties alice in wonderland
style.

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:13.479
Then you can totally play pai sho in there.

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:14.479
which reminds me.

00:05:14.479 --> 00:05:17.949
Number 2 - Bolin gets his ass handed to him
in Pai Sho by asami

00:05:17.949 --> 00:05:21.300
It’s not so much about them playing pai
sho against each other.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:24.030
Pai Sho is just a metaphor for Korra’s conflict
with Zaheer.

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:26.460
As well as Zaheer’s plot in general.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:28.480
it works on all levels.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:31.710
Korra for instance.

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:35.410
Asami says that in order to defeat your opponent,
first you have to know them.

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:41.130
Korra didn’t totally get to know Zaheer,
but I think in the next one or two episodes

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:45.070
she’ll figure him out and what his plan
really is.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:47.690
Then there’s the long game.

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:50.389
Careful planning and strategy.

00:05:50.389 --> 00:05:53.319
Zaheer and the Red Lotus have clearly been
planning on bringing down the governments

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:56.270
of the world for a long time.

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:58.090
Infiltrating aspects of society.

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:00.069
Unalaq was the wild card.

00:06:00.069 --> 00:06:02.930
Which was also an awesome WTF reveal.

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:06.860
Which leads me to my number 1 moment - Unalaq
was part of the Red Lotus

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:11.190
He was in on everything, but when the plot
to capture Korra went south, he covered up

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:14.460
his involvement and let Zaheer and the rest
of the group rot in jail.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:19.509
The Dark Avatar stuff was all his own doing,
he just went rogue on the Red Lotus.

00:06:19.509 --> 00:06:23.930
So this implies that the Red Lotus as an organization
isn’t evil, it’s just a group of fanatics

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:27.639
that are so stuck on bringing balance, that
every once and a while, one of them ends up

00:06:27.639 --> 00:06:28.949
hurting a lot of people.

00:06:28.949 --> 00:06:31.949
Or in the case of Unalaq, almost destroying
everyone everywhere.

00:06:31.949 --> 00:06:34.040
I still feel like we’re only getting half
the story.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:37.490
Zaheer said Korra would eventually find out
what his plan was.

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:42.819
He said he didn’t want to kill her, but
I think we heard him say the opposite of that

00:06:42.819 --> 00:06:43.990
in an earlier episode.

00:06:43.990 --> 00:06:46.050
So he might be saying contradictory things.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.920
Either way I don’t think he’s just another
Unalaq, he doesn’t care about personal power.

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:54.530
He just cares about destroying the old world
so that a better one can grow in it’s place.

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:57.370
Presumably, based on what he said about Avatar
Wan, he wants things to be more like they

00:06:57.370 --> 00:07:00.170
were before Raava and Vaatu were separated.

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:04.569
If he could find a way to bring the Lion Turtles
back I would totally fund his kickstarter.

00:07:04.569 --> 00:07:10.449
But let me know what your favorite moment
was and do you think that Souyin is involved

00:07:10.449 --> 00:07:11.449
with the Red Lotus?

00:07:11.449 --> 00:07:15.580
Remember, there are probably a lot of them
we haven’t met yet, supposedly they’ve

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:18.290
existed since just after the 100 year war.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:22.539
Overall I gave episode 9 an A minus for finally
explaining so many things.

00:07:22.539 --> 00:07:26.669
A lot of you guys had already been talking
about the Red Lotus just because of spoilers

00:07:26.669 --> 00:07:32.629
and info from future episodes but I really
like the way they used Pai Sho to inform their

00:07:32.629 --> 00:07:35.129
splinter group.

00:07:35.129 --> 00:07:45.330
I have a feeling the wiser members of the
White Lotus like Zuko will know more about

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:49.539
them, but we haven’t seen him in a while.

00:07:49.539 --> 00:07:53.080
In terms of the new characters, Henry Rollins
has been amazing as Zaheer.

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:54.220
He is so perfect for that role.

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:57.659
He’s a really interesting person in real
life if you’re not familiar with him.

00:07:57.659 --> 00:08:06.200
He goes way beyond being a musician.

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:10.509
The only thing I’m dissapointed about so
far is his companions, the other Team Zaheer

00:08:10.509 --> 00:08:13.330
people feel like they haven’t gotten their
origin story moments.

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:16.409
To be fair, we still haven’t gotten a full
Zaheer origin story either.

00:08:16.409 --> 00:08:19.470
We only know that at some point in his teenage
years he joined the Red Lotus.

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:22.830
We don’t understand why he’s so passionate
about their cause.

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:25.669
Did he lose someone close to him during the
100 year war?

00:08:25.669 --> 00:08:31.229
Is he related to someone in the order?

00:08:31.229 --> 00:08:34.720
It’s a bit of a twist this time, but I feel
like he and his team will end up trying to

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:38.450
yoink Korra from the Earth Queen and the Dai
Lee.

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:42.500
For a second I thought he might be using the
earth queen as a puppet to help topple the

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:47.850
governments of the world.

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:50.011
But now it seems like she’s a completely
separate entity.

00:08:50.011 --> 00:08:57.140
And here’s an interesting thought, Zaheer
is like the Joker of Book 3.

00:08:57.140 --> 00:09:02.070
He just wants to watch the world burn….so
that a new world can grow in it’s place.

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:04.190
But it reminds you a lot of Heath Ledger in
Dark Knight.

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:06.110
He’s just an agent of chaos.

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:09.780
Plus he looks like he used to play a joker
in Suyin’s circus group.

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:15.090
For everyone wondering what the deal is with
episodes going all digital.

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:24.770
Mike and Bryan actually said that Nickelodeon
had a plan in place before Book 3 came out

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:32.640
to release it digitally but then that got
changed, then it leaked, plans changed again

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:34.200
and on top of all that.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.710
Korra doesn’t really fit with their other
programming very well.

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:40.940
It’s not like Spongebob, so they’ve had
a much harder time marketing it.

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:45.560
As a result, Korra is all digital for the
remainder of book 3 and book 4.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:50.470
It will never air new episodes on TV again.

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:54.500
So here are the places you can watch it.

00:09:54.500 --> 00:10:00.730
Every Friday at 12PM Eastern Time, new episodes
are released on Nick dot com.

00:10:00.730 --> 00:10:05.410
You can also buy episodes in the Amazon store
and on iTunes.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:08.310
I would recommend you just watch them for
free on Nick dot com.

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:10.220
But if you live in another country and they’re
blocked.

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:11.420
Just use a VPN workaround.

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:17.450
There are tons of guides on google about how
to view blocked content from other countries.

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:21.690
So each new episode will air every week.

00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:24.630
There are no more breaks before the end of
book 3.

00:10:24.630 --> 00:10:28.570
We don’t have a release date for book 4
but they’ll probably announce something

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:30.960
during the finale.

